client.on('ready', () => {
  client.application.commands.create({
    name: 'ban',
    description: 'Bans a user from the server',
  });

  commandHandler.process(client.application.commands.create('ban {target: "user"}'), { guildId: 'guild_id' });
});
```

Replace `'guild_id'` with the ID of the server you want to add the slash command to.

6. Define your bot's event handlers for the `interactionCreate` event. This event is called every time a user interacts with a command in your Discord server.

```javascript
client.on('interactionCreate', async interaction => {
  if (!interaction.isCommand()) return;

  if (interaction.commandName === 'ban') {
    // Implement your ban command logic here
  }
